// Title: Registry Run key persistence via reg.exe
// MITRE: T1547.001 (Persistence, Privilege Escalation)
// Data source: SecurityEvent (EventID 4688, requires command line logging in process creation events)
// Severity: Medium
// Description: Detects reg.exe adding a value under a "...\CurrentVersion\Run" or "...\RunOnce" key,
//   which makes a program start at every logon. Matches the process command line of the reg.exe call.
//   Does not cover other ways to write the key (PowerShell Set-ItemProperty, direct API calls, regedit).
// False positives / Tuning: Installers and admin scripts legitimately write Run keys.
//   Tune by excluding known parent processes or known value names, and review the target program path.

SecurityEvent
| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
| where EventID == 4688
| where Process =~ "reg.exe"
| where CommandLine has "add" and CommandLine contains @"\CurrentVersion\Run"
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, SubjectUserName, ParentProcessName, NewProcessName, CommandLine
| order by TimeGenerated desc
